msgid "If set to `true`, it will result in the Quarkus writing the transformed application bytecode to the build tool's output directory. This is useful for post-build tools that need to scan the application bytecode - for example for offline code-coverage tools. For example, if using Maven, enabling this feature will result in the classes in `target/classes` being updated with the versions that result after Quarkus has applied its transformations. Setting this to `true` however, should be done with a lot of caution and only if subsequent builds are done in a clean environment (i.e. the build tool's output directory has been completely cleaned)."
